            <h2>Where Zerodha Excels</h2>
            <p>Zerodha Kite is unquestionably India's best <strong>trading interface</strong>. It offers advanced charting, fast order execution, a clean UI, and competitive brokerage. Zerodha Console also provides a solid P&L view and tax reports for holdings you've transacted on through them. If you're an active trader who primarily buys stocks via Zerodha, Console handles your trade history well.</p>

            <h2>Where Zerodha Falls Short for Wealth Tracking</h2>
            <p>The problem arises when your world grows beyond Zerodha. If you have SIPs running on <a href="/arthavi-vs-groww">Groww</a> or CAMS, older folios from an agent, or stocks on a second Demat account — Console becomes blind to all of it. Zerodha's XIRR calculation also shows <strong>simplified returns</strong>, not true cash-flow-based XIRR. For SIP investors, this gap between "absolute returns" and real XIRR can be as large as 8–12 percentage points.</p>

            <p>There is no Portfolio Health Score. No AI chat. No diversification analysis. Console is built to show you <em>what you traded</em>, not <em>how your wealth is structured</em>.</p>

            <h2>The Recommended Setup: Use Both</h2>
            <p>The highest-leverage setup for a Zerodha user:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Keep trading stocks and managing SIPs on Zerodha Kite + Coin.</li>
                <li>Every month, export your holdings CSV from <strong>Zerodha Console → Portfolio → Holdings</strong>.</li>
                <li>Import it into Arthavi alongside your mutual fund investment statement.</li>
                <li>Use Arthavi's Ask AI to ask: <em>"Is my portfolio beating Nifty 50?"</em> or <em>"Am I over-exposed to banking?"</em></li>
            </ol>
            <p>You get the best execution platform + the best analytics platform — at zero additional cost.</p>

