                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Can I use Arthavi and Zerodha together?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm">Yes — and this is the recommended setup. Trade on Zerodha Kite. Export your holdings CSV from Zerodha Console and import into Arthavi for unified tracking.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Does Zerodha have a Portfolio Health Score?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm">No. Zerodha Console shows basic holdings and P&L. Portfolio Health Score, Diversification Score, and Risk Score are Arthavi-exclusive features.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Which calculates XIRR better — Zerodha or Arthavi?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm">Arthavi uses per-transaction cash-flow XIRR — the mathematically correct method for SIP investors. Zerodha shows simplified absolute or CAGR-style returns.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Does Zerodha track mutual funds from all AMCs?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm">No. Zerodha Coin only tracks funds purchased through Coin. Arthavi consolidates all mutual funds from any AMC, broker, or physical folio via your investment statement (CAS).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Is Arthavi safe compared to Zerodha?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm">Both are safe in different ways. Arthavi never holds credentials — it only accepts exported files which are parsed locally. Zerodha requires your login for trading, which is standard for a broker.</p>
                </div>
